### ===========================================================================
### VROS optimization - Kafka end-to-end demo
### ===========================================================================
###
### Kafka is not an HTTP protocol. This file demonstrates the Kafka-backed
### optimization pipeline through the two HTTP surfaces that expose it:
###
###   1. VROS REST API
###      Each call publishes or consumes Kafka events internally:
###        POST /jobs        -> VROS publishes to vros.optimization.requests
###        GET  /jobs/{id}   -> state is fed by acks / progress / results
###        GET  /solution    -> read from the result event
###
###   2. Kafka UI internal HTTP API
###      The UI at http://localhost:8090 is backed by an HTTP API we can query
###      to inspect topics, partitions, replicas and offsets.
###
### Topology:
###
###   VROS API ──requests──► Kafka ──► optimization-worker
###       ▲                                │
###       └── acks / progress / results ◄──┘
###
### Topics:
###   vros.optimization.requests         6 partitions (key = jobId)
###   vros.optimization.requests-retry-0/1/2
###   vros.optimization.requests-dlt
###   vros.optimization.acks             3 partitions
###   vros.optimization.progress         3 partitions
###   vros.optimization.results          3 partitions
###   vros.optimization.results-retry-0/1
###   vros.optimization.results-dlt
###
### Prerequisites:
###   docker compose up -d db keycloak kafka kafka-ui
###   ./mvnw -q -DskipTests install
###   ./mvnw -pl vros-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
###   ./mvnw -pl optimization-worker spring-boot:run
###
###   Seed a scenario first (see http/scenarios.http) and set @scenarioId.
###   Kafka UI: http://localhost:8090  (cluster name: vros)
### ===========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@workerUrl = http://localhost:8082
@kafkaUiUrl = http://localhost:8090
@token =
@scenarioId = 1


### ===========================================================================
### 1. PRODUCE
### Submit a job. VROS writes an OptimizationRequestEvent to
### vros.optimization.requests with the jobId as the record key.
### ===========================================================================
# @name submit
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "scenarioId": {{scenarioId}}
}


### ===========================================================================
### 2. CONSUME / OBSERVE
### The worker consumes the request, publishes ACCEPTED + progress, and VROS
### consumes those events and updates the job. Poll this until COMPLETED.
### ===========================================================================
@jobId = {{submit.response.body.jobId}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ===========================================================================
### 3. RESULT
### The worker publishes OptimizationResultEvent to vros.optimization.results.
### VROS consumes it, stores the solution, and marks the job COMPLETED.
### Returns 409 until the result event has been consumed.
### ===========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs/{{jobId}}/solution
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ===========================================================================
### 4. LIST
### Every job listed here went through Kafka.
### ===========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs?scenarioId={{scenarioId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Failed jobs (for example, after a poison message reached the DLT).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/optimization/jobs?status=FAILED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ===========================================================================
### 5. WORKER-SIDE KAFKA METRICS
### vros.optimization.jobs.submitted = requests consumed
### vros.optimization.jobs.completed = results produced
### vros.optimization.inflight      = solver tasks currently executing
### ===========================================================================
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.submitted

###
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.completed

###
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.inflight

###
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.dead_lettered

###
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.solve.duration

### All available worker metrics (including kafka.* client meters).
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/metrics


### ===========================================================================
### 6. VROS-SIDE KAFKA METRICS
### vros.optimization.jobs.submitted  = requests produced to Kafka
### vros.optimization.progress.events = progress events consumed from Kafka
### ===========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.submitted

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.progress.events

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.completed

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics/vros.optimization.jobs.dead_lettered

### All available API metrics (including kafka.* client meters).
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics


### ===========================================================================
### 7. KAFKA UI HTTP API
### These are the HTTP endpoints behind http://localhost:8090.
### They are the UI's internal API, not a stable public contract, but they
### make it easy to demonstrate Kafka topics and offsets over HTTP.
### ===========================================================================

### List all topics with partition and replication counts.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics

### Inspect the requests topic: partitions, leaders, min/max offsets.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.requests

### Inspect the results topic. offsetMax should have advanced after step 3.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.results

### Inspect the acks topic.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.acks

### Inspect the progress topic.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.progress

### Inspect the request dead-letter topic.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.requests-dlt

### Inspect the result dead-letter topic.
GET {{kafkaUiUrl}}/api/clusters/vros/topics/vros.optimization.results-dlt


### ===========================================================================
### 8. HEALTH
### ===========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

###
GET {{workerUrl}}/actuator/health


### ===========================================================================
### 9. DIRECT KAFKA INSPECTION (not HTTP - run in a terminal)
### ===========================================================================
###
### Consume a topic and print keys + headers:
###
### docker compose exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
###   --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
###   --topic vros.optimization.requests \
###   --from-beginning \
###   --property print.key=true \
###   --property print.headers=true
###
### Replace the topic with any of:
###   vros.optimization.acks
###   vros.optimization.progress
###   vros.optimization.results
###   vros.optimization.requests-retry-0
###   vros.optimization.requests-dlt
###   vros.optimization.results-dlt
###
### Produce a poison message to exercise retry -> DLT:
### (use the key of an existing job; insert a QUEUED row first if needed)
###
### echo "<jobId>:not-json-poison" | docker compose exec -T kafka \
###   /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh \
###   --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
###   --topic vros.optimization.requests \
###   --reader-property parse.key=true \
###   --reader-property key.separator=:
###
### Then poll GET /api/v1/optimization/jobs/{jobId} until it becomes FAILED:
###   "Dead-lettered after retries: failed to deserialize"
###
### ===========================================================================
